A CONDITIONAL TAKES PADDING AROUND EVERY KEYWORD, and the host reads these as one construct:

A <% if [[Present]] %>padded<% endif %> conditional inline in prose.

An <%if [[Present]]%>first<%elseif [[Other]]%>second<%else%>third<%endif%> chain, where each arm
after the first reuses the same parser on a new filter condition.

AN OPEN CONSTRUCT STANDS LAST IN ITS CARRIER. Every line below one parses INSIDE its body, so a
closing keyword written under this paragraph would shut the specimen the carrier exists to hold.

THE GRAMMAR CLOSES WHAT THE HOST LEAVES OPEN. The conditional below never reaches an `<%endif%>`,
and the host records `unterminated-conditional` and recovers to the end of the source. The grammar
bleeds nothing past this file, so nothing here stands degenerate — the divergence lives in what a
reader gets TOLD, which `tools/recovery-witness.js` measures and no colour reveals.

